## Overview

UV is a fast Python package manager that replaces pip, poetry, and other legacy tools. This guide covers best practices learned from real-world implementation and debugging.

**Key Benefits of UV:**

- 10-100x faster than pip
- Lock file for reproducible builds
- Built-in virtual environment management
- Cross-platform support

## Core Principles

1. **Use UV for everything**: venv creation, dependency installation, package management
2. **Single source of truth**: `pyproject.toml` for dependencies
3. **Reproducibility**: `uv.lock` for exact dependency versions
4. **No legacy tools**: Remove Poetry, pipenv, pip-tools if present
5. **Cross-platform**: Scripts work on Windows, macOS, and Linux

## Setup Script Architecture

### Recommended Pattern: Wrapper + PowerShell

**Best Practice** (learned from doc-composer project):

#### setup.bat (Windows Wrapper - SIMPLE)

```batch
@echo off
REM Simple wrapper - NO complex logic here!

echo ==================================================
echo   Project Setup Script for Windows
echo ==================================================
echo.

REM Check if PowerShell is available
where powershell >nul 2>nul
if %errorlevel% neq 0 (
    echo ERROR: PowerShell is not installed or not in PATH
    pause
    exit /b 1
)

echo Running setup script with PowerShell...
echo.

REM Run PowerShell script with execution policy bypass
powershell.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File ".\setup.ps1" %*

if %errorlevel% neq 0 (
    echo.
    echo ERROR: Setup script failed with error code %errorlevel%
    pause
    exit /b %errorlevel%
)

echo.
echo Setup completed successfully!
pause
```

#### setup.ps1 (PowerShell - ALL LOGIC HERE)

```powershell
# Project Setup Script for Windows PowerShell
# All setup logic goes here - clean, maintainable, no encoding issues

param(
    [switch]$Force = $false
)

# CRITICAL: Use "Continue" not "Stop" for UV compatibility
$ErrorActionPreference = "Continue"

Write-Host "============================================" -ForegroundColor Cyan
Write-Host "   Project Setup" -ForegroundColor Cyan
Write-Host "============================================" -ForegroundColor Cyan
Write-Host ""

# ... all setup logic here ...
```

#### setup.sh (POSIX Shell - Cross-platform)

```bash
#!/bin/bash
# Project Setup Script for Linux/macOS

set -e  # Exit on error

echo "============================================"
echo "   Project Setup"
echo "============================================"
echo ""

# Python Version Detection
PYTHON_CMD=""
for cmd in python3 python; do
    if command -v "$cmd" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
        version=$("$cmd" -c "import sys; print(f'{sys.version_info.major}.{sys.version_info.minor}')" 2>/dev/null || echo "")
        if [ -n "$version" ]; then
            major=$(echo "$version" | cut -d. -f1)
            minor=$(echo "$version" | cut -d. -f2)
            if [ "$major" -eq 3 ] && [ "$minor" -ge 12 ]; then
                PYTHON_CMD="$cmd"
                echo "[1/4] Found Python $version using: $cmd"
                break
            fi
        fi
    fi
done

if [ -z "$PYTHON_CMD" ]; then
    echo "ERROR: Python 3.12+ not found!"
    echo "Download from: https://www.python.org/"
    exit 1
fi

# UV Installation Check
echo "[2/4] Checking UV installation..."
if ! command -v uv >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    echo "  UV not found. Installing..."
    # Download installer first, then execute
    TEMP_FILE=$(mktemp)
    if curl -fsSL https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh -o "$TEMP_FILE"; then
        # TODO: Add checksum verification per security policy
        chmod +x "$TEMP_FILE"
        "$TEMP_FILE"
        rm -f "$TEMP_FILE"
    else
        echo "  ERROR: Failed to download UV installer"
        exit 1
    fi
fi

# Virtual Environment Setup
echo "[3/4] Setting up virtual environment..."
if [ ! -d ".venv" ]; then
    uv venv --python "$PYTHON_CMD"
fi

# Dependency Installation
echo "[4/4] Installing dependencies..."
uv lock
uv sync

echo ""
echo "Setup completed successfully!"
```

### Why This Pattern?

✅ **Avoids encoding issues**: Windows batch files can't handle Unicode/emojis  
✅ **Better error handling**: PowerShell has proper try/catch  
✅ **Easier maintenance**: One language for all logic  
✅ **Cross-platform ready**: Separate `.sh` for Unix, same pattern  
✅ **No special character problems**: Pipes, redirects work properly

### AVOID: Complex Batch Files

❌ **Anti-pattern**: Putting complex logic in `.bat` files

```batch
# ❌ BAD: This causes "... was unexpected at this time" error
echo ✅ Success!

# ❌ BAD: Complex UV commands in batch
powershell -c "irm url | iex"  # Pipe parsed by batch!

# ✅ GOOD: Simple wrapper only
powershell.exe -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File ".\setup.ps1"
```

## Critical UV Error Handling

### ⚠️ The UV stderr Problem

**UV writes informational messages to stderr, which PowerShell treats as errors!**

This is the #1 cause of setup script failures.

#### ❌ WRONG Approaches

```powershell
# ❌ Still treats stderr as error
& uv sync 2>$null

# ❌ Fails on informational messages
& uv lock
# PowerShell sees "Resolved 162 packages in 2ms" on stderr and fails!
```

#### ✅ CORRECT Approach

```powershell
# ✅ BEST: Use "Continue" and assign output to $null
$ErrorActionPreference = "Continue"  # Not "Stop"!

# Assign output to $null (doesn't trigger error handling)
$null = & uv lock 2>&1
$null = & uv sync 2>&1
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit 1 }

# ✅ ALSO GOOD: Let UV output show, check exit code explicitly
& uv sync
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) {
    Write-Host "ERROR: UV sync failed" -ForegroundColor Red
    exit 1
}
```

#### Critical: ErrorActionPreference Setting

```powershell
# ❌ BAD: "Stop" treats stderr as terminating error
$ErrorActionPreference = "Stop"
& uv sync 2>&1 | Out-Null  # FAILS!

# ✅ GOOD: "Continue" allows checking $LASTEXITCODE
$ErrorActionPreference = "Continue"
$null = & uv sync 2>&1     # Works!
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit 1 }
```

#### Real-World Example (setup.ps1)

```powershell
# PowerShell script header - CRITICAL setting!
$ErrorActionPreference = "Continue"  # Not "Stop"!

# Install dependencies sequence
Write-Host "Installing dependencies..." -ForegroundColor Cyan

# Update lock file (writes to stderr on success!)
$null = & uv lock 2>&1

# Install base dependencies
$null = & uv sync 2>&1
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) {
    Write-Host "ERROR: Failed to install dependencies" -ForegroundColor Red
    exit 1
}

Write-Host "Dependencies installed successfully!" -ForegroundColor Green
```

## Common Pitfalls

### 1. Emoji Characters in Batch Files

**Problem**: Emoji characters in `.bat` files cause syntax errors.

```batch
# ❌ NEVER do this in .bat files
echo ✅ Done!
echo 📦 Installing...
echo ⚠️ Warning!

# ERROR: "... was unexpected at this time"
```

**Solution**: Use plain text or move to PowerShell

```batch
# ✅ Plain text in batch
echo Done!
echo Installing...
echo Warning!
```

```powershell
# ✅ Emojis work fine in PowerShell
Write-Host "Done!" -ForegroundColor Green
Write-Host "Installing..." -ForegroundColor Cyan
```

### 2. Pipe Character in Batch

**Problem**: Pipes `|` are interpreted by batch parser, not passed to PowerShell.

```batch
# ❌ BAD: Pipe is parsed by batch file
powershell -c "irm https://url | iex"
# ERROR: "| was unexpected at this time"

# ✅ GOOD: Use -Command with script block
powershell -Command "& {irm https://url | iex}"

# ✅ BETTER: Put command in .ps1 file
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File ".\install.ps1"
```

### 3. Double Dash Parameters

**Problem**: Double-dash parameters can cause issues in batch context.

```batch
# ❌ May fail in some contexts
uv --version

# ✅ Use call keyword
call uv --version

# ✅ Or use single-dash alias
uv -V
```

### 4. Treating Warnings as Errors

**Problem**: UV's informational output on stderr treated as fatal error.

```powershell
# ❌ Fails because UV writes to stderr
try {
    & uv sync
} catch {
    # This catches informational messages!
    exit 1
}

# ✅ Check exit code only
$null = & uv sync 2>&1
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) {
    exit 1
}
```

### 5. Not Handling Delayed Expansion

**Problem**: Variable expansion timing in batch files.

```batch
# ❌ BAD: Variable not expanded in loop
for %%f in (*.txt) do (
    set COUNT=%COUNT%+1
    echo %COUNT%  # Always shows initial value!
)

# ✅ GOOD: Enable delayed expansion
setlocal enabledelayedexpansion
for %%f in (*.txt) do (
    set /a COUNT+=1
    echo !COUNT!  # Use ! instead of %
)
```

## Python Version Detection

### Check Multiple Locations in Order

```powershell
function Test-PythonVersion {
    param([string]$PythonCmd)
    
    try {
        $version = & $PythonCmd -c "import sys; print(f'{sys.version_info.major}.{sys.version_info.minor}.{sys.version_info.micro}')" 2>$null
        if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) {
            $versionParts = $version -split '\.'
            $major = [int]$versionParts[0]
            $minor = [int]$versionParts[1]
            
            # Accept Python 3.12 or higher
            if ($major -eq 3 -and $minor -ge 12) {
                return @{
                    Valid = $true
                    Version = $version
                    Command = $PythonCmd
                }
            }
        }
    }
    catch {
        # Command not found
    }
    
    return @{ Valid = $false }
}
```

### Search Order

1. **PYTHON_EXE environment variable** (project-specific)
2. **Common commands**: `python`, `python3`, `py`
3. **Common installation paths**:
   - `C:\Python312\python.exe`
   - `C:\Program Files\Python312\python.exe`
   - `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\Python\Python312\python.exe`
4. **Fail with clear error** if not found

### Example Implementation

```powershell
Write-Host "[1/4] Checking for Python 3.12 or higher..." -ForegroundColor Cyan

$pythonCmd = $null

# 1. Check PYTHON_EXE
if ($env:PYTHON_EXE) {
    Write-Host "  Checking PYTHON_EXE environment variable..." -ForegroundColor Gray
    $result = Test-PythonVersion -PythonCmd $env:PYTHON_EXE
    if ($result.Valid) {
        $pythonCmd = $result.Command
        Write-Host "  Found Python $($result.Version)" -ForegroundColor Green
    }
}

# 2. Check common commands
if (-not $pythonCmd) {
    foreach ($cmd in @("python", "python3", "py")) {
        $result = Test-PythonVersion -PythonCmd $cmd
        if ($result.Valid) {
            $pythonCmd = $result.Command
            Write-Host "  Found Python $($result.Version) using: $cmd" -ForegroundColor Green
            break
        }
    }
}

# 3. Fail if not found
if (-not $pythonCmd) {
    Write-Host ""
    Write-Host "ERROR: Python 3.12+ not found!" -ForegroundColor Red
    Write-Host "Download from: https://www.python.org/" -ForegroundColor Yellow
    exit 1
}
```

## UV Installation

### Check and Auto-Install Pattern

```powershell
Write-Host "[2/4] Checking UV installation..." -ForegroundColor Cyan

$uvInstalled = Get-Command uv -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue

if (-not $uvInstalled) {
    Write-Host "  UV not found. Installing..." -ForegroundColor Yellow
    
    try {
        # Download installer first for security verification
        $tempFile = Join-Path $env:TEMP "uv-install.ps1"
        Invoke-WebRequest -Uri "https://astral.sh/uv/install.ps1" -OutFile $tempFile
        
        # TODO: Verify checksum/signature before execution per org policy
        # Example: $hash = Get-FileHash $tempFile -Algorithm SHA256
        # if ($hash.Hash -ne $expectedHash) { throw "Checksum mismatch" }
        
        # Execute installer
        . $tempFile
        Remove-Item $tempFile -Force
        
        # Refresh PATH for current session
        $env:PATH = [System.Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable("PATH", "User") + ";" + 
                    [System.Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable("PATH", "Machine")
        
        # Verify installation
        $uvInstalled = Get-Command uv -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
        if ($uvInstalled) {
            Write-Host "  UV installed successfully!" -ForegroundColor Green
        } else {
            Write-Host "  WARNING: UV installed but not in PATH" -ForegroundColor Yellow
            Write-Host "  Please restart your terminal" -ForegroundColor Yellow
        }
    }
    catch {
        Write-Host "  ERROR: Failed to install UV: $_" -ForegroundColor Red
        exit 1
    }
} else {
    Write-Host "  UV is already installed" -ForegroundColor Green
    $uvVersion = & uv --version 2>$null
    Write-Host "  Version: $uvVersion" -ForegroundColor Gray
}
```

## Virtual Environment Setup

### Standard UV Venv Pattern

```powershell
Write-Host "[3/4] Setting up virtual environment..." -ForegroundColor Cyan

if (Test-Path ".venv") {
    if ($Force) {
        Write-Host "  Removing existing .venv..." -ForegroundColor Yellow
        Remove-Item -Recurse -Force ".venv"
    } else {
        Write-Host "  Virtual environment already exists" -ForegroundColor Green
        
        # Verify Python version (accept >= 3.12)
        if (Test-Path ".venv\Scripts\python.exe") {
            $venvVersion = & ".venv\Scripts\python.exe" -c "import sys; print(f'{sys.version_info.major}.{sys.version_info.minor}')" 2>$null
            
            if ($venvVersion) {
                $parts = $venvVersion -split '\.'
                $major = [int]$parts[0]
                $minor = [int]$parts[1]
                
                if ($major -eq 3 -and $minor -ge 12) {
                    Write-Host "  Using existing Python $venvVersion venv" -ForegroundColor Green
                } else {
                    Write-Host "  WARNING: Venv is Python $venvVersion, requires >= 3.12" -ForegroundColor Yellow
                    Write-Host "  Run with -Force to recreate" -ForegroundColor Yellow
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

if (-not (Test-Path ".venv")) {
    Write-Host "  Creating new virtual environment..." -ForegroundColor Gray
    & uv venv --python $pythonCmd
    
    if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) {
        Write-Host "  ERROR: Failed to create venv" -ForegroundColor Red
        exit 1
    }
    
    Write-Host "  Virtual environment created!" -ForegroundColor Green
}
```

## Dependency Installation

### Installation Sequence

```powershell
Write-Host "[4/4] Installing dependencies..." -ForegroundColor Cyan

# 1. Update lock file (UV writes to stderr even on success!)
Write-Host "  Updating lock file..." -ForegroundColor Gray
$null = & uv lock 2>&1
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) {
    Write-Host "  ERROR: Failed to update lock file" -ForegroundColor Red
    exit 1
}

# 2. Install base dependencies
Write-Host "  Installing base dependencies..." -ForegroundColor Gray
$null = & uv sync 2>&1

if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) {
    Write-Host "  ERROR: Failed to install base dependencies" -ForegroundColor Red
    exit 1
}

Write-Host "  Base dependencies installed!" -ForegroundColor Green

# 3. Install optional extras
Write-Host "  Installing build tools..." -ForegroundColor Gray
$null = & uv sync --extra build 2>&1

if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) {
    Write-Host "  Build tools installed!" -ForegroundColor Green
} else {
    Write-Host "  WARNING: Some build tools failed" -ForegroundColor Yellow
}

# 4. Install Python version-specific extras (if needed)
$venvPython = ".venv\Scripts\python.exe"
$null = & $venvPython -c "import sys; sys.exit(0 if sys.version_info[:2] == (3, 12) else 1)" 2>&1

if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) {
    Write-Host "  Installing Python 3.12 extras..." -ForegroundColor Gray
    $null = & uv sync --extra pelia 2>&1
    
    if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) {
        Write-Host "  Python 3.12 extras installed!" -ForegroundColor Green
    } else {
        Write-Host "  WARNING: Some extras failed" -ForegroundColor Yellow
    }
}
```

## Build Scripts

### Build Script Requirements

1. **Verify spec file exists**: Don't proceed without spec file
2. **Use UV for tools**: `uv run --extra build tool`
3. **Auto-install dependencies**: Check and install if missing
4. **Clear error messages**: Tell users what to do
5. **Handle clean/rebuild**: Support clean builds

### Example Build Script (batch)

```batch
@echo off
REM Build script for Windows

:build
echo Building executable...

REM Check if spec file exists
if not exist "myapp.spec" (
    echo ERROR: Spec file "myapp.spec" not found!
    echo.
    echo The spec file should be in the project root.
    echo If missing, restore from version control.
    echo.
    exit /b 1
)

REM Ensure build dependencies are installed
echo Installing build dependencies...
call uv sync --extra build
if errorlevel 1 (
    echo ERROR: Failed to install build dependencies
    exit /b 1
)

REM Clean previous builds
echo Cleaning previous build artifacts...
if exist build rmdir /s /q build
if exist dist rmdir /s /q dist

REM Run PyInstaller through UV
echo Running PyInstaller...
uv run --extra build pyinstaller myapp.spec --noconfirm --clean

if errorlevel 1 (
    echo ERROR: Build failed!
    exit /b 1
)

echo Build completed successfully!
goto end

:end
```

### Build Script (PowerShell)

```powershell
# Build script for Windows PowerShell

Write-Host "Building executable..." -ForegroundColor Cyan

# Check spec file
if (-not (Test-Path "myapp.spec")) {
    Write-Host "ERROR: Spec file 'myapp.spec' not found!" -ForegroundColor Red
    Write-Host "Restore from version control" -ForegroundColor Yellow
    exit 1
}

# Install build dependencies
Write-Host "Installing build dependencies..." -ForegroundColor Gray
$null = & uv sync --extra build 2>&1

if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) {
    Write-Host "ERROR: Failed to install build dependencies" -ForegroundColor Red
    exit 1
}

# Clean previous builds
Write-Host "Cleaning previous builds..." -ForegroundColor Gray
if (Test-Path "build") { Remove-Item -Recurse -Force "build" }
if (Test-Path "dist") { Remove-Item -Recurse -Force "dist" }

# Run PyInstaller
Write-Host "Running PyInstaller..." -ForegroundColor Gray
& uv run --extra build pyinstaller myapp.spec --noconfirm --clean

if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) {
    Write-Host "ERROR: Build failed!" -ForegroundColor Red
    exit 1
}

Write-Host "Build completed successfully!" -ForegroundColor Green
```

## Testing Setup Scripts

### Manual Testing Checklist

Test your setup scripts in these scenarios:

- [ ] **Fresh install**: No `.venv` directory exists
- [ ] **Existing correct venv**: `.venv` with Python 3.12+
- [ ] **Existing wrong venv**: `.venv` with different Python version
- [ ] **UV installed**: UV already in PATH
- [ ] **UV not installed**: UV needs to be installed
- [ ] **Python in PATH**: `python` command works
- [ ] **Python via PYTHON_EXE**: Only `$env:PYTHON_EXE` set
- [ ] **Different directories**: Run from subdirectories
- [ ] **Fresh terminal**: After install, before PATH refresh
- [ ] **With -Force flag**: Force recreation of venv

### Automated Testing

```powershell
# test_setup.ps1
Write-Host "Testing setup script..." -ForegroundColor Cyan

# Test 1: Python detection
$result = Test-PythonVersion -PythonCmd "python"
if (-not $result.Valid) {
    Write-Host "FAIL: Python detection" -ForegroundColor Red
    exit 1
}
Write-Host "PASS: Python detection" -ForegroundColor Green

# Test 2: UV available
$uv = Get-Command uv -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
if (-not $uv) {
    Write-Host "FAIL: UV not found" -ForegroundColor Red
    exit 1
}
Write-Host "PASS: UV found" -ForegroundColor Green

# Test 3: Venv created
if (-not (Test-Path ".venv")) {
    Write-Host "FAIL: Venv not created" -ForegroundColor Red
    exit 1
}
Write-Host "PASS: Venv created" -ForegroundColor Green

# Test 4: Dependencies installed (generic test)
$testImport = & ".venv\Scripts\python.exe" -c "import sys; print('OK')" 2>$null
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) {
    Write-Host "FAIL: Dependencies not installed" -ForegroundColor Red
    exit 1
}
Write-Host "PASS: Dependencies installed" -ForegroundColor Green

Write-Host ""
Write-Host "All tests passed!" -ForegroundColor Green
```

## Command Reference

### UV Common Commands

```bash
# Virtual Environment
uv venv                           # Create venv with system Python
uv venv --python python3.12       # Create with specific Python version
uv venv --python /path/to/python  # Create with Python at path

# Dependency Installation
uv sync                           # Install base dependencies
uv sync --extra build             # Install with 'build' extra
uv sync --all-extras              # Install all extras
uv lock                           # Update lock file

# Running Python
uv run python script.py           # Run Python in venv
uv run --extra build pyinstaller  # Run with extra dependencies
uv run pytest                     # Run pytest in venv

# Package Management
uv add package-name               # Add dependency to pyproject.toml
uv add --dev package-name         # Add dev dependency
uv remove package-name            # Remove dependency
uv pip list                       # List installed packages
uv pip show package-name          # Show package info

# Other
uv --version                      # Show UV version
uv -V                            # Short version
uv help                          # Show help
```

### pyproject.toml Structure

```toml
[project]
name = "your-project"
version = "0.1.0"
description = "Project description"
requires-python = ">=3.12"
dependencies = [
    "package>=1.0.0",
    # ... core dependencies
]

[project.optional-dependencies]
build = [
    "PyInstaller>=6.0.0",
    # ... build tools
]
dev = [
    "pytest>=7.0.0",
    # ... development tools
]

[tool.uv]
# UV-specific configuration (optional)

[build-system]
requires = ["hatchling"]
build-backend = "hatchling.build"
```

## Troubleshooting

### Issue: "... was unexpected at this time"

**Cause**: Emoji or special Unicode characters in batch file

**Solution**: Remove emojis or move logic to PowerShell

```batch
# ❌ Causes error
echo ✅ Done

# ✅ Fix
echo Done
```

### Issue: Setup fails with "Resolved X packages" error

**Cause**: UV writes informational messages to stderr, which PowerShell treats as errors when `$ErrorActionPreference = "Stop"`

**Error Message**:

```
uv.exe : Resolved 162 packages in 2ms
At setup.ps1:173 char:1
+ & uv lock 2>&1 | Out-Null
+ ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
   + CategoryInfo          : NotSpecified: (Resolved 162 packages...)
   + FullyQualifiedErrorId : NativeCommandError
```

**Solution (BEST)**: Use `$ErrorActionPreference = "Continue"` and assign to `$null`

```powershell
# ✅ BEST: Set proper error preference
$ErrorActionPreference = "Continue"  # Not "Stop"!

# Assign output to $null (doesn't trigger error handling)
$null = & uv lock 2>&1
$null = & uv sync 2>&1

# Check exit code explicitly
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) {
    Write-Host "ERROR: UV failed" -ForegroundColor Red
    exit 1
}
```

### Issue: UV not found after installation

**Cause**: PATH not refreshed in current session

**Solution**: Refresh PATH or restart terminal

```powershell
# Refresh PATH
$env:PATH = [System.Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable("PATH", "User") + ";" +
            [System.Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable("PATH", "Machine")

# Or just restart terminal
```

### Issue: Wrong Python version in venv

**Cause**: Venv created with different Python

**Solution**: Recreate with correct Python

```powershell
# Delete and recreate
Remove-Item -Recurse -Force ".venv"
uv venv --python python3.12
```

### Issue: Build fails "PyInstaller not found"

**Cause**: Build extras not installed

**Solution**: Install build dependencies

```bash
uv sync --extra build
```

### Issue: Pipe character causes batch error

**Cause**: Pipe parsed by batch, not PowerShell

**Solution**: Use `-Command` with script block

```batch
# ❌ Fails
powershell -c "cmd | other"

# ✅ Fix
powershell -Command "& {cmd | other}"
```

